{"episodes":{"156377":"An isolated severe thunderstorm produced golf ball sized hail during the evening hours.","157187":"Gusty winds in excess of 34 knots occurred on the back edge of a large area of rain with a few thunderstorms, possibly associated with a wake low.","157631":"A stationary cold front draped to the south of the region and potent upper level disturbances approaching from Northern Mexico caused increasing wind shear and instability across portions of West Central Texas.  These features triggered isolated elevated severe thunderstorms near Abilene on April 14.  On April 15, more severe thunderstorms resulted in several large to very large hail storms.","157636":"An unsettled weather pattern during the week of April 12th generated several days of showers and thunderstorms across North and Central Texas, as multiple upper level disturbances moved across the region. A few of these storms produced large hail.","157875":"A stalled frontal boundary combined with sufficient instability in place produced a thunderstorm over Lake Ponchartrain resulting in a couple severe wind reports.","157876":"A line of thunderstorms moving along a stalled frontal boundary draped across the coastal waters and produced a sustained line of marine severe wind reports.","157879":"A line of thunderstorms moving along a stalled frontal boundary draped across the coastal waters produced localized flash flooding and hail.","157880":"A line of thunderstorms moving along a stalled frontal boundary draped across the coastal waters produced heavy rainfall resulting in flash flooding.","157893":"Thunderstorms developed along a stationary front and moved through northeastern parts of South Central Texas. The airmass these storms encountered favored supercell development and they produced large hail.","158148":"Scattered severe thunderstorms in advance of a cold front produced damaging winds and large hail across portions of northeast North Carolina.","158273":"Elevated strong to severe thunderstorms developed across inland southeast Mississippi early in the morning on April 15th. There were a couple of reports of severe hail associated with these storms.","158274":"Scattered to numerous thunderstorms developed across southwest Alabama ahead of a strong spring time storm system. The storms produced an isolated severe hail event along with flash flooding in the metro Mobile area."},"events":[{"begin":"2021-04-15T00:07Z","county":"Northampton","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"2.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-15T00:07Z","endLat":36.45,"endLon":-77.57,"episode":158148,"id":956025,"injuries":0,"lat":36.45,"location":"Garysburg","lon":-77.57,"magnitude":50.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Trees were downed along Route 46 near Garysburg. Power outages were reported in the area.","source":"Utility Company","state":"NC","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"AKQ"},{"begin":"2021-04-15T00:34Z","county":"Northampton","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-15T00:34Z","endLat":36.27,"endLon":-77.29,"episode":158148,"id":956024,"injuries":0,"lat":36.27,"location":"0.56 W Rich Square","lon":-77.29,"magnitude":1.75,"narrative":"Golf ball size hail was reported.","source":"Public","state":"NC","type":"Hail","wfo":"AKQ"},{"begin":"2021-04-15T01:10Z","county":"Bertie","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"5.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-15T01:10Z","endLat":36.11,"endLon":-76.94,"episode":158148,"id":956026,"injuries":0,"lat":36.11,"location":"0.89 SE Askewville","lon":-76.94,"magnitude":2.75,"narrative":"Baseball size hail was reported in Askewville.","source":"Public","state":"NC","type":"Hail","wfo":"AKQ"},{"begin":"2021-04-15T01:43Z","county":"Washington","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-15T01:43Z","endLat":35.9354,"endLon":-76.6305,"episode":156377,"id":944231,"injuries":0,"lat":35.9354,"location":"0.69 WNW Mackeys","lon":-76.6305,"magnitude":1.75,"narrative":"Golf ball sized hail fel